    "result_text": "All tests pass. The project contains a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` feature so owners are assigned a code formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` on creation.\n\n**What each part does:**\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter so the value is persisted and read back on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in the create path (`addOwner`), assigns the code via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper before saving:\n  - `LAST3` = first three letters of `lastName`, upper-cased (guarded with `Math.min(3, length)` for short names).\n  - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits \u2014 a **global** sequence equal to one more than the current owner count. Because the first owner is persisted (and auto-flushed) before the second's count query runs, the second code is exactly the first + 1, satisfying the test's `SMI-` / `JON-` global-sequence assertion.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps the same-named entity property through to the response (no mapper change needed).\n- **Schema files** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four DB schemas (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`); the tests run on `hsqldb`, which was the source of the initial `InvalidDataAccessResourceUsageException` before I added the column there. The column is nullable so existing seed inserts remain valid.\n\n**Test result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
